WEBVTT

1
00:00:26.041 --> 00:00:30.250


2
00:00:30.250 --> 00:00:31.666
<b>Here Lord Krishna,</b>

3
00:00:31.666 --> 00:00:34.791
<b>addressing Arjuna, says,</b>

4
00:00:34.791 --> 00:00:36.333
<b>"O Partha!</b>

5
00:00:36.333 --> 00:00:41.750
<b>How can one who considers this soul</b>
<b>to be unborn, eternal, indestructible,</b>

6
00:00:41.750 --> 00:00:43.791
<b>cause anyone to be killed,</b>

7
00:00:43.791 --> 00:00:44.541
<b>or</b>

8
00:00:44.541 --> 00:00:46.125
<b>kill?"</b>

9
00:00:46.791 --> 00:00:51.000


10
00:00:51.000 --> 00:00:56.041
<b>Arjuna's greatest anguish was about</b>
<b>the death of kinsmen in war,</b>

11
00:00:56.041 --> 00:00:57.791
<b>and his bigger fear was that</b>

12
00:00:57.791 --> 00:01:01.208
<b>this death would perhaps come</b>
<b>by his own hands</b>

13
00:01:01.208 --> 00:01:01.916
<b>and</b>

14
00:01:01.916 --> 00:01:03.958
<b>be called murder.</b>

15
00:01:03.958 --> 00:01:06.958
<b>Krishna wants to explain here that, Arjuna,</b>

16
00:01:06.958 --> 00:01:10.291
<b>when you understand this</b>
<b>supreme knowledge of the soul,</b>

17
00:01:10.291 --> 00:01:14.166
<b>you'll know that the soul cannot die,</b>

18
00:01:14.166 --> 00:01:16.083
<b>and if death hasn't occurred at all,</b>

19
00:01:16.083 --> 00:01:20.125
<b>then where is the question</b>
<b>of murder by your hands?</b>

20
00:01:20.125 --> 00:01:21.416
<b>Krishna is speaking,</b>

21
00:01:21.416 --> 00:01:24.375
<b>and Arjuna is listening silently,</b>

22
00:01:24.375 --> 00:01:26.708
<b>absorbing these words.</b>

23
00:01:26.708 --> 00:01:30.583
<b>All these points are meant to resolve his doubts.</b>

24
00:01:30.583 --> 00:01:33.291
<b>Krishna here also wants to convey</b>

25
00:01:33.291 --> 00:01:36.250
<b>that the soul performs no physical action,</b>

26
00:01:36.250 --> 00:01:38.625
<b>it simply exists,</b>

27
00:01:38.625 --> 00:01:39.916
<b>it was,</b>

28
00:01:39.916 --> 00:01:41.666
<b>and it will remain.</b>

29
00:01:42.375 --> 00:01:46.416


30
00:01:46.416 --> 00:01:53.791
<b>Rarely does a human see themselves</b>
<b>beyond their physical form.</b>

31
00:01:53.791 --> 00:01:57.875
<b>Yet herein lies a paradox...</b>

32
00:01:57.875 --> 00:02:01.958
<b>Man identifies completely with his body,</b>

33
00:02:01.958 --> 00:02:08.666
<b>and he knows well that this</b>
<b>body is destined to perish.</b>

34
00:02:08.666 --> 00:02:14.625
<b>Yet he refuses to accept this destruction.</b>
<b>He yearns to live eternally.</b>

35
00:02:14.625 --> 00:02:15.875
<b>My friend,</b>

36
00:02:15.875 --> 00:02:18.208
<b>isn't this like saying,</b>

37
00:02:18.208 --> 00:02:24.958
<b>"I want to bathe in water,</b>
<b>but I don't want to get wet"?</b>

38
00:02:24.958 --> 00:02:27.500
<b>What a contradiction this is</b>

39
00:02:27.500 --> 00:02:29.333
<b>to cling to the body,</b>

40
00:02:29.333 --> 00:02:33.166
<b>yet deny its mortality.</b>

41
00:02:33.166 --> 00:02:34.875
<b>But</b>

42
00:02:34.875 --> 00:02:39.833
<b>perhaps there's a deeper meaning</b>
<b>hidden in this paradox?</b>

43
00:02:39.833 --> 00:02:41.250
<b>Consider this</b>

44
00:02:41.250 --> 00:02:47.416
<b>where does this inclination</b>
<b>to live eternally come from?</b>

45
00:02:47.416 --> 00:02:49.458
<b>Could it be</b>

46
00:02:49.458 --> 00:02:55.708
<b>that this is a glimpse of your spiritual nature?</b>

47
00:02:55.708 --> 00:02:56.833
<b>The Soul.</b>

48
00:02:56.833 --> 00:02:58.375
<b>Eternal.</b>

49
00:02:58.375 --> 00:03:01.416
<b>Indestructible.</b>

50
00:03:01.416 --> 00:03:09.416
<b>For those who see life only through a material</b>
<b>lens, this wisdom may be difficult to grasp.</b>

51
00:03:09.416 --> 00:03:10.125
<b>But</b>

52
00:03:10.125 --> 00:03:12.375
<b>gradually, each layer will unfold,</b>

53
00:03:12.375 --> 00:03:15.375
<b>all doubts shall fade away.</b>

54
00:03:16.000 --> 00:03:20.416


55
00:03:20.416 --> 00:03:22.166
<b>Great is Arjun's dilemma</b>

56
00:03:22.166 --> 00:03:23.791
<b>before him lies a great war,</b>

57
00:03:23.791 --> 00:03:25.041
<b>weapons will clash,</b>

58
00:03:25.041 --> 00:03:29.500
<b>many bodies will fall.</b>

59
00:03:29.500 --> 00:03:33.958
<b>My effort is to make him understand</b>
<b>this supreme truth:</b>

60
00:03:33.958 --> 00:03:37.000
<b>that man's true form is the soul,</b>

61
00:03:37.000 --> 00:03:39.291
<b>which no one can destroy.</b>

62
00:03:39.291 --> 00:03:43.416
<b>So why grieve for that which cannot die?</b>

63
00:03:43.416 --> 00:03:48.041
<b>Why be anxious about</b>
<b>something that never happened?</b>

64
00:03:48.041 --> 00:03:49.125
<b>Tell me,</b>

65
00:03:49.125 --> 00:03:50.333
<b>is it right</b>

66
00:03:50.333 --> 00:03:53.958
<b>to worry about something</b>
<b>that hasn't even occurred?</b>

67
00:03:53.958 --> 00:03:55.583
<b>Of course not.</b>

68
00:03:55.583 --> 00:03:58.875
<b>Now, think again</b>

69
00:03:58.875 --> 00:04:04.916
<b>don't we ourselves become anxious</b>
<b>about things that haven't even happened?</b>

70
00:04:04.916 --> 00:04:06.708
<b>Someone spoke ill of you?</b>

71
00:04:06.708 --> 00:04:12.041
<b>But did their words actually make you bad?</b>

72
00:04:12.041 --> 00:04:13.291
<b>No, right?</b>

73
00:04:13.291 --> 00:04:19.000
<b>Then why anger over something</b>
<b>that never happened? Why the anxiety?</b>

74
00:04:19.000 --> 00:04:27.541
<b>It's like white color getting angry</b>
<b>because someone called it blue.</b>

75
00:04:27.541 --> 00:04:35.875
<b>White remained white, didn't it? Did someone's</b>
<b>words actually turn it blue?</b>

76
00:04:35.875 --> 00:04:37.375
<b>Therefore,</b>

77
00:04:37.375 --> 00:04:42.083
<b>don't accept the harsh words thrown at you.</b>

78
00:04:42.083 --> 00:04:47.916
<b>No one can hurt you without your acceptance.</b>

79
00:04:47.916 --> 00:04:50.291
<b>How powerful is this thought.</b>

80
00:04:50.291 --> 00:04:51.375
<b>Reflect on it.</b>

81
00:04:54.250 --> 00:04:56.166


82
00:04:56.166 --> 00:05:05.625
<b>When you live by spiritual values, you</b>
<b>no longer yearn to do wrong.</b>

83
00:05:05.625 --> 00:05:09.958
<b>The very tendency towards evil dissolves.</b>

84
00:05:09.958 --> 00:05:11.333
<b>Why is this so?</b>

85
00:05:11.333 --> 00:05:14.291
<b>Think for a moment</b>

86
00:05:14.291 --> 00:05:17.583
<b>when is one motivated to do wrong?</b>

87
00:05:17.583 --> 00:05:25.541
<b>or when they search for opportunities</b>
<b>to satisfy physical or financial temptations.</b>

88
00:05:25.541 --> 00:05:27.000
<b>But</b>

89
00:05:27.000 --> 00:05:31.458
<b>if your existence is eternal, indestructible,</b>

90
00:05:31.458 --> 00:05:35.291
<b>if you are beyond both time and senses,</b>

91
00:05:35.291 --> 00:05:41.250
<b>then how can any evil motivation,</b>
<b>any temptation even arise?</b>

92
00:05:41.250 --> 00:05:44.333
<b>Man knows very well what is right and wrong.</b>

93
00:05:44.333 --> 00:05:49.583
<b>He merely closes his eyes when doing wrong.</b>

94
00:05:49.583 --> 00:05:52.833
<b>And this is the very purpose of spirituality,</b>

95
00:05:52.833 --> 00:05:54.541
<b>of self-knowledge</b>

96
00:05:54.541 --> 00:05:56.625
<b>that your eyes remain open,</b>

97
00:05:56.625 --> 00:05:59.500
<b>that you become conscious in body and mind,</b>

98
00:05:59.500 --> 00:06:00.250
<b>and</b>

99
00:06:00.250 --> 00:06:04.041
<b>that evil tendencies may never lead you astray.</b>

